WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
In the time of Emperor Taizong of Tang, Songtsen Gampo, the ruler of Tibet, unified the plateau and hoped for a marriage alliance with the Tang.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:13.814
An envoy brought gifts to Chang'an to seek the marriage.

00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:23.788
Emperor Taizong married Princess Wencheng, a daughter of the imperial clan, into Tibet; the young princess bade farewell to Chang'an and journeyed west.

00:00:24.138 --> 00:00:27.858
The farewell procession stretched beyond the city gate.

00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:35.600
The princess brought seeds, craftsmen and books from the Central Plains, passing advanced techniques to the Tibetan people.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.550
The Tibetan people gathered around curiously to learn.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:46.428
Songtsen Gampo built the Potala Palace for the princess, and the two treated each other with respect and courtesy.

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:55.130
Princess Wencheng promoted friendly exchanges between the Tang and Tibet, and her story became a beloved tale told through the ages.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.864
This story has been passed down for more than a thousand years.

